---
/** @fileoverview Renders the docs landing page with product benefits and rule examples. */
import AgentPreview from './AgentPreview.astro';
import CodeTransformation from './CodeTransformation.astro';
import CodeSample from './CodeSample.astro';
import RuleApplication from './RuleApplication.astro';
import exampleRule from '../examples/verify-retry-limits.md?raw';
---
<section class="cr-hero" aria-labelledby="_top">
  <p class="cr-eyebrow">FABRICA / CODE RULES</p>
  <h1 id="_top" data-page-title>The package manager<br class="desktop-break" /> for your engineering rules</h1>
  <p class="cr-lead">Version your best practices. Import them across projects.<br />Show your agents how to write good code, then validate it.</p>
  <div class="cr-actions">
    <a class="cr-button primary" href="/guides/use-rules/">Set up Code Rules <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    <a class="cr-button" href="/overview/">Read the docs <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
  </div>
</section>
<AgentPreview />
<section aria-label="How Code Rules works">
  <article class="cr-feature">
    <div>
      <span class="cr-index">01 / CODIFY</span>
      <h2>Define the practices your agents should follow.</h2>
      <p>Write rules in Markdown to tell agents how to write and validate code. Cover technologies like Go or React, and practices like testing, error handling, or logging.</p>
      <a href="/guides/write-rules/">Learn how to write rules →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="cr-panel cr-rule-file">
      <header class="cr-file-header">
        <span class="cr-index">EXAMPLE RULE</span>
        <div class="cr-rule-path"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="16" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8Z" /><path d="M14 2v6h6" /></svg><span>practices/testing/verify-retry-limits.md</span></div>
      </header>
      <CodeSample code={exampleRule.trimEnd()} lang="md" tone="vivid" label="Example rule with YAML frontmatter and Markdown guidance" />
    </div>
  </article>
  <article class="cr-feature">
    <div>
      <span class="cr-index">02 / SHARE</span>
      <h2>Declare rules for a single repo, or an entire organization.</h2>
      <p>Each repo keeps its rules in <code>.code-rules</code>. Publish shared defaults from an organization <code>.code-rules</code> repository and import them. Combine shared and project-specific rules so agents have the right guidance in each repo.</p>
      <a href="/concepts/libraries/">See how rule libraries work →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="cr-panel cr-library-tree">
      <span class="cr-index">EXAMPLE RULE LIBRARY</span>
      <div class="cr-tree-root">acme/.code-rules/</div>
      <pre aria-label="Example library with 8 Markdown rules organized into four technology and practice groups"><code><span class="cr-tree-branch" aria-hidden="true">├── </span><span class="cr-tree-meta">rule-library.json</span>
<span class="cr-tree-branch" aria-hidden="true">├── </span><span class="cr-tree-folder">techs/</span>
<span class="cr-tree-branch" aria-hidden="true">│   ├── </span><span class="cr-tree-folder">typescript/</span>
<span class="cr-tree-branch" aria-hidden="true">│   │   ├── </span><span class="cr-tree-meta">_group.json</span>
<span class="cr-tree-branch" aria-hidden="true">│   │   ├── </span><span class="cr-tree-file">narrow-unknown-values.md</span>
<span class="cr-tree-branch" aria-hidden="true">│   │   └── </span><span class="cr-tree-file">model-valid-states.md</span>
<span class="cr-tree-branch" aria-hidden="true">│   └── </span><span class="cr-tree-folder">react/</span>
<span class="cr-tree-branch" aria-hidden="true">│       ├── </span><span class="cr-tree-meta">_group.json</span>
<span class="cr-tree-branch" aria-hidden="true">│       ├── </span><span class="cr-tree-file">keep-state-local.md</span>
<span class="cr-tree-branch" aria-hidden="true">│       └── </span><span class="cr-tree-file">name-interactive-controls.md</span>
<span class="cr-tree-branch" aria-hidden="true">└── </span><span class="cr-tree-folder">practices/</span>
<span class="cr-tree-branch" aria-hidden="true">    ├── </span><span class="cr-tree-folder">testing/</span>
<span class="cr-tree-branch" aria-hidden="true">    │   ├── </span><span class="cr-tree-meta">_group.json</span>
<span class="cr-tree-branch" aria-hidden="true">    │   ├── </span><span class="cr-tree-file">verify-retry-limits.md</span>
<span class="cr-tree-branch" aria-hidden="true">    │   └── </span><span class="cr-tree-file">test-failure-paths.md</span>
<span class="cr-tree-branch" aria-hidden="true">    └── </span><span class="cr-tree-folder">error-handling/</span>
<span class="cr-tree-branch" aria-hidden="true">        ├── </span><span class="cr-tree-meta">_group.json</span>
<span class="cr-tree-branch" aria-hidden="true">        ├── </span><span class="cr-tree-file">preserve-error-context.md</span>
<span class="cr-tree-branch" aria-hidden="true">        └── </span><span class="cr-tree-file">bound-retries.md</span></code></pre>
    </div>
  </article>
  <article class="cr-feature">
    <div>
      <span class="cr-index">03 / APPLY</span>
      <h2>Make your rules part of your agent’s workflow.</h2>
      <p>Add instructions to your project’s AGENTS.md, or your agent’s equivalent, telling it where to find your rules and when to read them. Your agent uses those rules when writing and reviewing code.</p>
      <a href="/for-agents/">See how agents use rules →</a>
    </div>
    <RuleApplication />
  </article>
</section>
<CodeTransformation />
<section class="cr-start" aria-labelledby="start-title"><span class="cr-index">START WITH ONE PROJECT</span><h2 id="start-title">Give your agents rules for good code</h2><p>Choose your project’s rules, then set up your agents to use them when writing and validating code.</p><a class="cr-button" href="/guides/use-rules/">Walk through the setup <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section>
